;; The appliance on a Compute Module 5, official IO board.
;;
;; The same device as the Pi 3 and Pi Zero images serve - Modbus, OPC UA,
;; CAN on vcan0, MQTT, config over HTTP - on the board a CM5 development kit
;; ships with. This is the one to build first, because it is the carrier
;; that exists on the desk rather than in a listing.
;;
;; When the industrial carriers arrive, the same three lines with
;; target:cm5-io swapped for target:cm5-io-wireless give a board with real
;; RS485 and a real CAN bus, and the build is a minute rather than an hour,
;; because everything below the carrier is already in the store.

(image cm5-io-appliance
  (compose
    image:cm5-io
    feature:dev-ssh
    feature:modbus
    feature:fieldbus-test)
  (verified-against (buildroot "2025.02.16")))
